WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:59.580
<b>A Beautiful World</b>

3
00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:02.920
Marines

4
00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:05.790
This is the current Navy Headquarters,

5
00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:08.040
led by the newly-promoted
Fleet Admiral Sakazuki.

6
00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:10.050
"New Marineford."

7
00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:13.130
Two years ago, in the War of the Best,

8
00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:16.970
Navy forces battled against
the Whitebeard Pirates.

9
00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:19.140
The skirmish ended
in the Navy's victory.

10
00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:23.730
However, the destruction
to Marineford was quite catastrophic.

11
00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:27.010
The original base functioned as

12
00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:28.090
the heart of the
world's justice system,

13
00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:31.000
but in order to acclimate
to the raging Pirate Era,

14
00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:35.340
the World Government constructed
an even greater fortress.

15
00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:40.470
New Marineford has
become the new home of justice,

16
00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:43.640
located at the entrance
to the New World.

17
00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:50.550
Fujitora dared to show
his face in Mary Geoise?

18
00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:52.480
Yes! I'm afraid so, sir!

19
00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:56.510
He was only to step foot in
a base under one condition!

20
00:01:56.510 --> 00:01:59.640
By bringing me the heads
of Straw Hat and Law!

21
00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:02.990
I thought I was extremely clear with
what I told him back in Dressrosa.

22
00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:05.160
What's his excuse?

23
00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:06.830
Wow, scary.

24
00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:09.400
How dare he come back here
like nothing happened!

25
00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:10.440
What a jackass!

26
00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:11.820
I'm sorry.

27
00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:14.070
I'm afraid I don't have
any answers for you, sir!

28
00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:16.990
Then tell me why didn't
you boot his ass, huh?

29
00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:21.750
Well, he was armed with theoretical
rhetoric and we were powerless, sir!

30
00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:27.030
If you ask me, it's fair game,
since this isn't military ground.

31
00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:30.500
That yokel is just splitting hairs!

32
00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:32.580
Take him with
a grain of salt next time!

33
00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:35.940
Huh?

34
00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:36.960
Oh? Huh?

35
00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:39.730
It's a tough job, huh?

36
00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:42.680
Fleet Admiral.

37
00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:44.640
Se-Sengoku!

38
00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:48.560
You stay outta this,
you semi-retired has-been!

39
00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:53.990
So tell me, who else do
we have at Mary Geoise?

40
00:02:53.990 --> 00:02:56.660
A-Admiral Ryokugyu, sir!

41
00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.280
Ryokugyu, huh?

42
00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:01.160
Then contact him immediately!

43
00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:01.950
Yes, sir!

44
00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:05.880
Even though the position of Navy
Headquarters has changed,

45
00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:08.760
New Marineford still
serves the same purpose.

46
00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:13.060
Guarding the gates of Mary Geoise
where the Celestial Dragons reside.

47
00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:16.350
The location of the previous base,
where the War of the Best took place,

48
00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:19.560
has become the home of the G-1 Branch.

49
00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:25.310
<b>The Holy Land</b>
<b>Mary Geoise</b>
<b>Old Marineford</b>
<b>(Current G-1 Branch)</b>
<b>New Marineford</b>

50
00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:22.770
The two bases are situated
on either side of the Red Line,

51
00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:25.530
to protect Mary Geoise from attack.

52
00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:25.690
<b>(Current G-1 Branch) Old Marineford</b>

53
00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:25.980
<b>(Current G-1 Branch)</b>

54
00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:26.230
<b>Mary Geoise</b>

55
00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:26.140
<b>New Marineford</b>

56
00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:26.190
<b>The Holy Land</b>

57
00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:25.850
<b>Mary Geoise (Current G-1 Branch) Old Marineford</b>

58
00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:25.810
<b>Mary Geoise Old Marineford</b>

59
00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:26.060
<b>Mary Geoise (Current G-1 Branch)</b>

60
00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:26.020
<b>The Holy Land (Current G-1 Branch) Old Marineford</b>

61
00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:25.980
<b>Mary Geoise The Holy Land</b>

62
00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:26.060
<b>Old Marineford</b>

63
00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:35.030
This place is known as Red Port.

64
00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:38.200
<b>The Red Port</b>

65
00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:40.870
Like the Navy bases, each side of the Red
Line also has its own massive harbor.

66
00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:45.750
The Government has a novel means of crossing
the wall that always draws attention.

67
00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:47.920
Bondola 1, now departing.

68
00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:52.420
Look, Dad! It's going up!

69
00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:59.150
Bondolas, bubble-based gondolas, make
their way up to the Holy Land of Mary Geoise

70
00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:03.370
every day.

71
00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:05.330
They're here!

72
00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:07.660
Just look at all those
ships pouring in!

73
00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:23.830
Clear the way!
The royals are coming through!

74
00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:25.680
It's Beer the Sixth!

75
00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:28.100
Of the Roshwan Kingdom!

76
00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:32.900
And he brought
the Matryoshesses! How cute!

77
00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:36.150
Queen
Morollon of the Tajine Kingdom!

78
00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:37.860
She's so beautiful!

79
00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:40.700
Here's a toast to all
the lovely eyes in the world!

80
00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:45.350
It's better to die standing,
than live on your knees!

81
00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:47.430
King Taco from the Kingdom of the Dead!

82
00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:51.930
Look! King Ham Burger of the
Ballywood Kingdom just showed up!

83
00:04:56.390 --> 00:04:58.810
Is there a reason
why he's walking so slow?

84
00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:07.700
Although my pace may
be measured, I vow.

85
00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:10.490
I will never turn back!

86
00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:22.470
Huh? A Navy ship?

87
00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:35.370
Whoa! He made it!

88
00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:39.330
It's the Great Knight
of the Sea, King Neptune!

89
00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:42.380
And look! The
three princes are with him, too!

90
00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:45.920
The Ryugu Kingdom's
finally here for the Reverie!

91
00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:47.550
Prince Fukaboshi!

92
00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:52.710
I'm bringing the party
wherever I stand!

93
00:05:56.070 --> 00:05:57.320
Are you two ready for this?

94
00:05:57.320 --> 00:05:58.990
I was born ready!

95
00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:02.120
Garp, yoo-hoo!

96
00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:09.060
<b>Vice Admiral Monkey D. Garp
(Luffy's Grandfather)
Marine Headquarters</b>

97
00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:09.180
<b>Palace</b>

98
00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:09.140
<b>Ryugu</b>

99
00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:07.560
Damn! Thought I was
gonna drown down there!

100
00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:12.230
<b>Ryugu</b>

101
00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:09.430
<b>Ryugu Palace</b>

102
00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:12.230
<b>Palace</b>

103
00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:12.230
Hey! Miss Princess! Come on out!

104
00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:16.810
We can do this, Shirahoshi.

105
00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:20.070
Together! Let's go to Mary Geoise!

106
00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:24.490
Yes.

107
00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:29.530
It's beautiful!

108
00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:42.590
It has been 200 years
since the Ryugu Kingdom

109
00:06:42.590 --> 00:06:45.170
began its affiliation with
the World Government.

110
00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:49.340
But in all that time, they've
attended the Reverie only once before.

111
00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:53.020
So this is indeed a rare occasion!

112
00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:56.730
<b>Kamabakka Queendom
Peachy Island</b>

113
00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:01.410
I wouldn't blame you if you had mixed
feelings about our little plan, Koala.

114
00:07:01.410 --> 00:07:03.120
With the Fishmen, I mean.

115
00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:05.160
Must be tough.

116
00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:08.870
They make it to the Reverie
and then we invade it.

117
00:07:08.870 --> 00:07:13.750
It's fine. And besides, the Reverie
isn't what we have a problem with,

118
00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:15.960
or even the World Government.

119
00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:17.760
It's just the Celestial Dragons.

120
00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:19.690
They're our enemy.

121
00:07:23.690 --> 00:07:24.820
Welcome!

122
00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:28.030
We're all so excited to have you here!

123
00:07:43.610 --> 00:07:44.960
She's so big and beautiful!

124
00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:49.090
Fire! Just like a dream!

125
00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:56.340
Hey, Boss. She deserves
a feature story, right?

126
00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:58.790
Princess Shirahoshi!

127
00:07:59.150 --> 00:08:00.860
Is he gonna be okay?

128
00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:04.110
Forget it. He can't even hear us.

129
00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:05.900
We love you, Princess!

130
00:08:07.950 --> 00:08:09.730
Garp, I'm worried.

131
00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:12.270
She seems to be a bit too popular.

132
00:08:12.270 --> 00:08:14.980
Folks have been looking
forward to this for days.

133
00:08:14.980 --> 00:08:19.440
Rumors were spreading, saying your daughter
was as beautiful as the Pirate Empress.

134
00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:23.680
She's gonna be a bonafide
celebrity, I'm afraid!

135
00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:25.480
She is awfully pretty.

136
00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:27.310
Not to mention huge.

137
00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:29.360
So everyone gets a good look!

138
00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:39.180
Hm?

139
00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:41.970
That thing over there.
What's it called?

140
00:08:41.970 --> 00:08:44.140
Would it happen to be a forest?

141
00:08:44.140 --> 00:08:46.350
No, that's just a tree.

142
00:08:48.890 --> 00:08:51.890
Well! It's the great hero, Garp!

143
00:08:55.610 --> 00:08:58.980
And you must know who
I am, needless to say.

144
00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:01.930
Yeah you're some stupid brat,
now outta my way.

145
00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:05.230
What was that? I must have heard wrong!

146
00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:06.990
He isn't joking, is he?

147
00:09:06.990 --> 00:09:09.140
Unless he isn't-isn't joking, that is!

148
00:09:09.140 --> 00:09:10.600
How dare you!

149
00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:14.560
I'm Sterry, king of the Goa
Kingdom, from whence you hail!

150
00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:18.620
<b>King Sterry
(Sabo's Adopted Brother)
Kingdom of Goa, East Blue</b>

151
00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:16.190
You know what that means?

152
00:09:16.190 --> 00:09:19.100
As one of my subjects,
you answer to me!

153
00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:23.590
I'll let you off this time, but you would
do well to remember that in the future!

154
00:09:24.530 --> 00:09:29.540
Sterry was taken in by Sabo's
parents, who are nobles.

155
00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:35.620
With that as a foothold, he and his new
family schemed to improve his standing

156
00:09:35.620 --> 00:09:39.090
and wed him to Princess Isntoinette.

157
00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:41.590
Later, the king and the prince
of the Goa Kingdom

158
00:09:41.590 --> 00:09:43.670
both mysteriously died.

159
00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:47.980
<b>High Town</b>
<b>Mount
Colubo</b>
<b>Midtown</b>
<b>Windmill
Village</b>
<b>Gray 
Terminal</b>
<b>Edge Town</b>
<b>Palace</b>

160
00:09:43.670 --> 00:09:48.120
And as a result, several months
ago, Sterry rose to power.

161
00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:50.670
Didn't expect those two to meet up.

162
00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:55.630
Goa is a simple and quiet place,
but it's home to a fair number of outlaws.

163
00:09:55.630 --> 00:09:57.260
Garp's the exception here.

164
00:09:57.260 --> 00:10:00.130
It was home to the leader of
the Revolutionary Army.

165
00:10:00.130 --> 00:10:02.120
Their Second-in-Command, too.

166
00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:03.540
Roger's son, Ace.

167
00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:04.810
And Straw Hat.

168
00:10:04.810 --> 00:10:07.560
There's something special
about that place!

169
00:10:07.560 --> 00:10:10.870
Now, if you'd like to apologize
by kneeling at my feet.

170
00:10:10.870 --> 00:10:12.250
Please do.

171
00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:15.330
Piss off, brat. I got places to be.

172
00:10:16.580 --> 00:10:19.590
The audacity of this man confounds me!

173
00:10:22.280 --> 00:10:24.620
Let me cut to the chase, Garp.

174
00:10:24.620 --> 00:10:25.830
Hm?

175
00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:28.290
I need connections, my good man.

176
00:10:28.290 --> 00:10:31.620
Pull some strings so I can
become a Celestial Dragon.

177
00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:33.400
They're all scumbags, you know.

178
00:10:35.700 --> 00:10:37.450
What?!

179
00:10:37.710 --> 00:10:39.920
Uh-oh! I hope nobody heard that!

180
00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:42.060
We'll be put to death at this rate!

181
00:10:42.060 --> 00:10:44.640
Wait. Not s'posed to say that.

182
00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:46.100
I take it back.

183
00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:49.660
He's terrifying!

184
00:10:49.660 --> 00:10:50.910
Hm?

185
00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:56.580
There you are, young man.

186
00:10:56.580 --> 00:10:58.790
Are you all right?

187
00:10:58.790 --> 00:11:02.590
That thing can move?
I thought that was a statue!

188
00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:04.210
Is he a Giant?

189
00:11:04.210 --> 00:11:10.120
I heard they eat humans and can
melt rocks with their saliva.

190
00:11:11.650 --> 00:11:13.280
No, wait. What are these things?

191
00:11:14.450 --> 00:11:15.650
Fangs? Scales?

192
00:11:15.990 --> 00:11:18.160
Look at the colors of their skin!

193
00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:19.910
They must be Fishmen!

194
00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:22.460
More fish than man, for certain!

195
00:11:22.460 --> 00:11:24.370
They're undersea abominations!

196
00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:27.460
Beasts who spread disease
to humans by mere contact!

197
00:11:27.460 --> 00:11:29.800
Don't touch me!

198
00:11:35.760 --> 00:11:39.060
Bondola 2, now departing.

199
00:11:44.230 --> 00:11:46.650
So long! You folks take it easy!

200
00:11:46.650 --> 00:11:49.070
Thank you, Mister Luffy's Grandpa, sir!

201
00:11:49.070 --> 00:11:50.980
It was fun traveling with you!

202
00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:54.320
I can't wait to see more
of the surface world!

203
00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:18.260
We're so high! It's like a dream!

204
00:12:18.720 --> 00:12:22.680
Hm? Is something
the matter, dear daughter?

205
00:12:28.980 --> 00:12:32.900
The sun. I can hardly believe it.

206
00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:39.200
Indeed.

207
00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:48.080
sparkling in the sunlight,
like dancing jewels!

208
00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:53.000
Gotta admit,
it makes me wanna mambo!

209
00:12:55.340 --> 00:12:59.220
I never knew that such a beautiful
world was waiting for us!

210
00:12:59.220 --> 00:13:02.800
It's like I'm seeing
the light for the first time.

211
00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:08.270
I must admit, the sun tree on
the ocean floor pales in comparison.

212
00:13:14.150 --> 00:13:17.280
This is where I want to be, Father.

213
00:13:17.280 --> 00:13:22.200
If I can, I wish to stay here
on the surface.

214
00:13:22.200 --> 00:13:25.820
And I want to show this
dazzling world, bathed in light,

215
00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:28.200
to all the people
of our kingdom as well!

216
00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:31.960
I'll ask them.

217
00:13:31.960 --> 00:13:35.040
That's what the Reverie
is all about, after all.

218
00:13:34.710 --> 00:13:37.380
<b>The Holy Land
Mary Geoise</b>

219
00:13:42.930 --> 00:13:48.140
For the record, Sakazuki told
me to find you and kick you out.

220
00:13:51.190 --> 00:13:52.940
Do you want to fight?

221
00:13:52.940 --> 00:13:56.230
Yeah, no thank you.

222
00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:58.570
I think I'll pass on that!

223
00:13:58.570 --> 00:14:02.240
Besides, it's not like you're gonna
destroy the conference, right?

224
00:14:02.240 --> 00:14:03.980
Not at all.

225
00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:08.110
But there is something
I do want to destroy.

226
00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:10.200
The system.

227
00:14:11.990 --> 00:14:14.240
That aside, thanks for the meal.

228
00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:15.860
It was fine, indeed.

229
00:14:15.860 --> 00:14:18.170
You traveled a long way to get here.

230
00:14:18.170 --> 00:14:20.680
How is old man Vegapunk doing?

231
00:14:20.680 --> 00:14:23.890
Well. Not that I
could see it, of course,

232
00:14:23.890 --> 00:14:26.970
but he's got quite
a creation on his hands.

233
00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:29.230
You want to give me a clue?

234
00:14:31.310 --> 00:14:33.690
We won't need the Seven Warlords.

235
00:14:33.690 --> 00:14:35.990
Not anymore.

236
00:14:35.990 --> 00:14:41.490
Off your rocker,
as usual! I love it!

237
00:14:41.490 --> 00:14:46.070
I'll say it once more,
the food here truly is excellent.

238
00:14:46.070 --> 00:14:48.240
I noticed you haven't
had a single bite.

239
00:14:48.240 --> 00:14:51.610
Am I to assume that
you're still on your fast?

240
00:14:49.330 --> 00:14:55.580
<b>Admiral Ryokugyu
Marine Headquarters</b>

241
00:14:51.610 --> 00:14:53.280
If I went "ahhh,"

242
00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:58.170
and a fine woman put
some food in, I'd eat.

243
00:14:58.170 --> 00:15:02.420
But that's not happening, so I haven't
eaten a thing in three years or so!

244
00:15:04.010 --> 00:15:08.510
<b>The Red Line</b>

245
00:15:09.180 --> 00:15:12.680
Help! Stop the wind!

246
00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:15.180
It's scary!

247
00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:25.070
Simmer down, lad.

248
00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:27.820
Whoa, whoa,
whoa, whoa, did you see that?

249
00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:29.860
I don't know what you're referrin' to.

250
00:15:29.860 --> 00:15:32.280
A Giant! He was in the wall!

251
00:15:32.280 --> 00:15:36.910
Just staring at us w-with some
kind of trident and a dumb hat!

252
00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:38.870
You must be hallucinating.

253
00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:41.160
Why would a face be
lurking in a mountain?

254
00:15:41.160 --> 00:15:43.460
I know what I saw!

255
00:15:45.060 --> 00:15:46.230
Why are there so many crows?

256
00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:48.210
And they're huge!

257
00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:50.590
Rare to see them up this high!

258
00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:55.400
So these must be "birds"!

259
00:15:55.400 --> 00:15:58.310
How cute! They really can fly!

260
00:15:58.310 --> 00:16:00.900
If they peck at the bubble,
we'll fall and die!

261
00:16:00.900 --> 00:16:02.320
Go away!

262
00:16:02.320 --> 00:16:04.110
You there, come here!

263
00:16:04.110 --> 00:16:06.910
Do your job! Shoot down these crows!

264
00:16:06.910 --> 00:16:09.200
This is a clear safety hazard!

265
00:16:10.950 --> 00:16:12.280
Don't worry, King Sterry.

266
00:16:12.620 --> 00:16:14.160
You'll be fine.

267
00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:16.210
Just you wait and see.

268
00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:21.590
Riding a Bondola, they travel high up
to Mary Geoise at the top of the Red Line.

269
00:16:22.700 --> 00:16:24.660
I hope you had a pleasant trip.

270
00:16:26.300 --> 00:16:28.300
Please watch your step.

271
00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:32.720
Merfolk!

272
00:16:34.130 --> 00:16:35.250
The atmospheric
pressure is different here,

273
00:16:35.740 --> 00:16:37.650
so please use these reinforced bubbles.

274
00:16:38.980 --> 00:16:39.900
Why thank you!

275
00:16:41.490 --> 00:16:43.790
It's huge!

276
00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:48.460
From here, the guests ascend
a long and extravagant staircase,

277
00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:52.050
leading to a land that lies at
the center of all four seas.

278
00:16:52.050 --> 00:16:56.350
It is the largest continent in the world
and rests at the highest altitude.

279
00:16:57.940 --> 00:17:00.480
I think I need a piggy-back ride.

280
00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:04.040
We're almost there, King Sterry.

281
00:17:15.520 --> 00:17:20.150
The descendants of those who created
the world itself reside here.

282
00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:23.360
And the name of this beautiful place...

283
00:17:24.650 --> 00:17:26.940
the Holy Land of Mary Geoise.

284
00:17:29.510 --> 00:17:32.010
I want to live here. Pretty please?

285
00:17:34.810 --> 00:17:36.810
It's such a lovely place!

286
00:17:36.810 --> 00:17:39.480
Is that green spot there
a forest, perhaps?

287
00:17:39.480 --> 00:17:41.280
It's man-made, but yes.

288
00:17:41.280 --> 00:17:43.740
So this is it. Mary Geoise.

289
00:17:46.820 --> 00:17:50.620
Looks like it's still
quite a trek to the castle.

290
00:17:50.620 --> 00:17:52.500
Please, come this way.

291
00:17:56.680 --> 00:17:59.720
Take these handles and
hold on, if you would.

292
00:18:05.930 --> 00:18:07.760
An earthquake!

293
00:18:07.760 --> 00:18:10.470
The ground's moving on its own!

294
00:18:12.290 --> 00:18:13.700
This is called a "Travelator."

295
00:18:15.150 --> 00:18:17.190
The pathway will carry you.

296
00:18:17.970 --> 00:18:22.140
Father, perhaps we
should follow this side path?

297
00:18:22.140 --> 00:18:25.150
Shirahoshi, you wanted to
look at the forest, didn't you?

298
00:18:25.540 --> 00:18:26.670
Fukaboshi.

299
00:18:27.700 --> 00:18:29.830
Isn't the scenery beautiful here?

300
00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:31.320
Better for us to take our time.

301
00:18:31.320 --> 00:18:33.970
Ooh! I think that's a wonderful idea!

302
00:18:33.970 --> 00:18:36.760
Father, you don't mind if
we stroll for a bit, do you?

303
00:18:36.760 --> 00:18:38.620
It would be my pleasure.

304
00:18:38.620 --> 00:18:40.280
We shall escort you.

305
00:18:41.140 --> 00:18:44.190
Heh. Those stupid fish!
Afraid of modern technology!

306
00:18:44.620 --> 00:18:46.530
Bunch of savages!

307
00:18:46.530 --> 00:18:49.330
I simply must procure
one of these for my kingdom!

308
00:18:49.330 --> 00:18:50.960
The Troubleator, you say?

309
00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:52.670
"Travelator," actually.

310
00:18:52.670 --> 00:18:54.960
Call it what you like!

311
00:18:56.340 --> 00:19:00.880
I don't know why,
but something feels wrong here.

312
00:19:00.490 --> 00:19:04.410
<b>Underground</b>

313
00:19:04.570 --> 00:19:06.320
Not too fast, not too slow.

314
00:19:07.260 --> 00:19:08.630
Make it nice and easy!

315
00:19:08.630 --> 00:19:11.010
Keep the pace steady, you fools!

316
00:19:13.030 --> 00:19:15.530
If you stop, then you get the whip!

317
00:19:18.410 --> 00:19:22.160
Someone save me! Or at least kill me!

318
00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:26.230
<b>A Certain Celestial Dragon's Mansion</b>

319
00:19:26.500 --> 00:19:29.580
Father! Lookie! Lookie!

320
00:19:29.580 --> 00:19:31.150
What's wrong, Charloss?

321
00:19:31.150 --> 00:19:34.990
It's a mermaid! And she's big, too!

322
00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:48.460
Open the gate!

323
00:19:58.010 --> 00:20:01.140
<b>A Courtyard Within the Castle</b>

324
00:20:02.970 --> 00:20:07.730
It would appear that all the royal families
have brought their bodyguards with them.

325
00:20:07.730 --> 00:20:12.190
They aren't armed,
but they look rather formidable.

326
00:20:12.190 --> 00:20:14.740
They have quite
the feast laid out for us!

327
00:20:14.740 --> 00:20:16.990
It'll be nothing but
conferences for seven days,

328
00:20:16.990 --> 00:20:20.890
starting tomorrow, so the leaders
better have fun while they can!

329
00:20:20.890 --> 00:20:22.730
Though I suppose the other guests just

330
00:20:22.730 --> 00:20:26.350
get to par-ti-la-so-fa-mi-re-do!

331
00:20:27.340 --> 00:20:30.550
I'm the King of Samba,
and in my land, Samba's King!

332
00:20:30.550 --> 00:20:32.180
Would you like to dance with me?

333
00:20:32.180 --> 00:20:33.390
Samba!

334
00:20:33.390 --> 00:20:36.670
Can't samba, but I can mambo!

335
00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:38.290
-Mambo, mambo! -Samba, samba!

336
00:20:38.290 --> 00:20:40.090
– Shake it, shake it! Shake it, shake it!
– Shake it, shake it! Shake it, shake it!

337
00:20:40.090 --> 00:20:45.400
Seems Father is getting along
well with everyone. That's good.

338
00:20:45.400 --> 00:20:47.400
Uh, um...

339
00:20:47.400 --> 00:20:48.620
– Huh?
– Huh?

340
00:20:48.620 --> 00:20:51.720
Can I help you?

341
00:20:51.720 --> 00:20:53.100
So the rumors are true!

342
00:20:53.100 --> 00:20:56.230
You are breathtakingly
beautiful, my dear!

343
00:20:56.230 --> 00:20:58.650
Might I introduce you to my son?

344
00:20:58.650 --> 00:21:00.060
He's single, you know!

345
00:21:00.060 --> 00:21:03.130
Wow. She's not bad, Papan, not bad!

346
00:21:03.130 --> 00:21:03.830
Oh. I, uh...

347
00:21:03.830 --> 00:21:06.060
Princess, my handsome son
here is a prince,

348
00:21:07.380 --> 00:21:08.890
and you might be a good match!

349
00:21:08.890 --> 00:21:11.930
Pappy. I like the big lady a lot!

350
00:21:11.930 --> 00:21:13.270
Oh. I...

351
00:21:13.270 --> 00:21:17.020
If you're looking for a prince, then
surely you can't do better than my boy!

352
00:21:17.020 --> 00:21:20.490
I have
three handsome princes who would

353
00:21:20.490 --> 00:21:23.530
love to have a chat with you!

354
00:21:23.530 --> 00:21:26.640
– Princess! Which one do you like best?
– Princess! Which one do you like best?

355
00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:28.600
I... Oh...

356
00:21:28.600 --> 00:21:29.140
No, um...

357
00:21:32.810 --> 00:21:36.320
I'm sorry, but, uh...

358
00:21:36.320 --> 00:21:37.730
None of you are my type!

359
00:21:37.730 --> 00:21:41.610
– Why not? They're princes, aren't they?
– Why not? They're princes, aren't they?

360
00:21:44.530 --> 00:21:48.120
Damn it! How dare you humiliate me!

361
00:21:48.870 --> 00:21:50.960
No, she was saying
"I'm not married, either"

362
00:21:50.960 --> 00:21:52.790
in an undersea dialect.

363
00:21:52.790 --> 00:21:55.590
This is all a misunderstanding!
She was merely using...

364
00:21:55.590 --> 00:21:57.250
What did I do wrong?

365
00:21:57.250 --> 00:21:59.130
When this happens,
just say something like,

366
00:21:59.130 --> 00:22:01.760
"How lovely, but I can't
possibly choose"!

367
00:22:01.760 --> 00:22:03.970
Gotta let them down softly, okay?

368
00:22:04.500 --> 00:22:06.420
But if I told them that,

369
00:22:06.420 --> 00:22:07.520
then I would be lying!

370
00:22:07.520 --> 00:22:10.010
It's not lying, it's redirecting.

371
00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:13.530
Better than starting a diplomatic
emergency, now let's go!

372
00:22:13.530 --> 00:22:15.150
So-la-ti-do!

373
00:22:18.200 --> 00:22:21.080
How cute!

374
00:22:20.240 --> 00:22:24.320
<b>Princess Vivi and Karoo
Kingdom of Arabasta</b>

375
00:22:21.080 --> 00:22:22.830
You're a like a little fairy!

376
00:22:22.830 --> 00:22:24.580
I could just eat you up!

377
00:22:24.490 --> 00:22:27.990
<b>Commander Leo
Tonta Corps, Tontatta Tribe</b>

378
00:22:24.580 --> 00:22:28.590
I'm a warrior, I'll have you know,
so that is not a compliment!

379
00:22:28.370 --> 00:22:31.370
<b>Mansherry</b>
<b>Kabu</b>
<b>Bian</b>

380
00:22:29.330 --> 00:22:31.370
You okay there, Leo?

381
00:22:31.470 --> 00:22:33.310
I didn't mean anything by it!

382
00:22:33.310 --> 00:22:34.810
Sorry I insulted you!

383
00:22:34.810 --> 00:22:38.120
Huh? Well, then that's okay!

384
00:22:38.120 --> 00:22:40.710
He's safe! She is nice after all!

385
00:22:40.710 --> 00:22:42.920
You certainly can move fast!

386
00:22:42.920 --> 00:22:45.850
I didn't notice at all
until Karoo spotted you.

387
00:22:45.850 --> 00:22:50.230
I allowed myself to be seen because I heard
that you were friends with Luffyland.

388
00:22:50.230 --> 00:22:53.360
We are the Straw Hat's
subordinates, you know!

389
00:22:53.360 --> 00:22:55.070
And we're pirates, too!

390
00:22:55.070 --> 00:22:57.400
Little pirates?

391
00:22:57.400 --> 00:22:58.610
That's so cute!

392
00:22:59.380 --> 00:23:01.590
A pleasure to meet you, as well!

393
00:23:02.710 --> 00:23:04.710
This is such a nice surprise.

394
00:23:04.710 --> 00:23:06.040
I wasn't expecting to meet so many

395
00:23:06.500 --> 00:23:08.260
of Lucy's friends at the Reverie!

396
00:23:08.990 --> 00:23:14.710
<b>Rebecca
A Dressrosan Lady-in-Waiting</b>

397
00:23:09.140 --> 00:23:12.940
But then again, the Straw Hats are
traveling the world, I suppose!

398
00:23:12.940 --> 00:23:15.350
Did Lucy visit your country as well?

399
00:23:15.350 --> 00:23:17.190
Or Luffy, I mean.

400
00:23:17.190 --> 00:23:20.270
Yeah! Tell us!

401
00:23:20.270 --> 00:23:23.690
He did. In fact, if it wasn't for them,

402
00:23:23.690 --> 00:23:27.950
the Kingdom of Alabasta
wouldn't even exist today.

403
00:23:27.950 --> 00:23:32.830
Princess Vivi from Alabasta, a desert
kingdom located on the Grand Line.

404
00:23:32.830 --> 00:23:35.660
She encountered the Straw Hats
more than two years ago

405
00:23:35.660 --> 00:23:39.300
and traveled on their ship as
a close friend for some time.

406
00:23:39.940 --> 00:23:42.860
Crocodile, who was a
Warlord of the Sea at the time,

407
00:23:42.860 --> 00:23:45.300
looked to take control of Alabasta.

408
00:23:45.300 --> 00:23:47.340
As a result, the kingdom
was locked in civil war

409
00:23:47.340 --> 00:23:50.460
between the royal army
and rebel forces.

410
00:23:50.460 --> 00:23:53.710
Crocodile's plot was
thwarted by Luffy and friends.

411
00:23:53.710 --> 00:23:56.760
At last, the Alabasta
Kingdom was saved.

412
00:23:56.760 --> 00:24:00.630
However, the World Government
reported the Navy was responsible,

413
00:24:00.630 --> 00:24:03.890
to hide the fact that
pirates won the day.

414
00:24:04.510 --> 00:24:07.220
They don't like to be seen as heroes.

415
00:24:07.870 --> 00:24:10.250
Their bounties keep getting
higher and higher.

416
00:24:10.250 --> 00:24:12.920
The whole world prob'ly
knows about them now.

417
00:24:12.920 --> 00:24:16.470
Still, they haven't changed
one bit, my friends.

418
00:24:16.470 --> 00:24:19.510
When I read about what happened
in Dressrosa, I knew.

419
00:24:19.510 --> 00:24:21.130
They saw someone in need.

420
00:24:21.130 --> 00:24:25.650
So I'll bet they did everything in
their power to save them, right?

421
00:24:25.650 --> 00:24:28.110
– Yeah! He did!
– Yeah! He did!

422
00:24:28.950 --> 00:24:31.240
Luffy did more than just save me.

423
00:24:31.240 --> 00:24:33.200
He saved our kingdom.

424
00:24:33.200 --> 00:24:35.910
The Straw Hats are the
heroes of all Dressrosa!

425
00:24:40.250 --> 00:24:42.590
I miss you, Lucy.

426
00:24:44.730 --> 00:24:46.890
Excuse me.

427
00:24:46.890 --> 00:24:51.390
Uhm, were the two of you talking
about Mister Luffy just now?

428
00:24:51.390 --> 00:24:54.210
The Mermaid Princess!

429
00:24:54.210 --> 00:24:56.290
Shirahoshi!

430
00:24:56.290 --> 00:24:58.710
Talking about him
doesn't mean they know him!

431
00:24:58.710 --> 00:25:00.840
Luffy's still a pirate, after all!

432
00:25:00.840 --> 00:25:03.510
You musn't let people know
he's your friend!

433
00:25:05.250 --> 00:25:07.460
The Mermaid Princess knows Luffy?

434
00:25:07.460 --> 00:25:10.250
Wait, you were asking
if we're friends with Luffy?

435
00:25:10.250 --> 00:25:13.170
Hold on, Rebecca!
You shouldn't say too much!

436
00:25:13.170 --> 00:25:16.760
Yes! I was right!
So you were talking about him!

437
00:25:16.760 --> 00:25:19.600
Stop it! Maybe they
were saying how bad he is!

438
00:25:19.600 --> 00:25:23.400
I... owe a great
debt of gratitude to Luffy.

439
00:25:26.350 --> 00:25:27.600
– Us, too!
– Us, too!

440
00:25:49.240 --> 00:25:53.110
Oh, speaking of Luffy,
he sure eats a lot, doesn't he?

441
00:25:53.380 --> 00:25:56.760
Yeah! If he's not eating,
he's prob'ly thinking about it!

442
00:25:57.390 --> 00:26:00.140
He certainly enjoys
a good feast, doesn't he?

443
00:26:00.140 --> 00:26:02.280
Seems they're having fun.

444
00:26:02.280 --> 00:26:03.830
That they are.

445
00:26:03.830 --> 00:26:06.700
I would say this bodes well
for the future of our nations!

446
00:26:06.700 --> 00:26:09.170
We've made good friends
in no time at all!

447
00:26:09.170 --> 00:26:12.090
Though I admit,
it's a strange connection.

448
00:26:12.090 --> 00:26:13.520
Indeed!

449
00:26:13.520 --> 00:26:16.710
Royal families united by the
goodwill of the Straw Hats!

450
00:26:16.710 --> 00:26:21.510
Excuse me! Aren't
you Rebecca from Dressrosa?

451
00:26:21.510 --> 00:26:22.760
– Huh?
– Huh?

452
00:26:22.760 --> 00:26:25.380
Wow! Look who it is!

453
00:26:25.190 --> 00:26:26.650
It's me, Sai!

454
00:26:25.400 --> 00:26:30.400
<b>Sai
13th Don of the Happo Navy</b>

455
00:26:26.960 --> 00:26:31.300
Funny! Feels like the last time I ran
into you was just the other day!

456
00:26:31.300 --> 00:26:33.790
- And have you been well?
– Better than ever!

457
00:26:33.790 --> 00:26:37.090
It seems he's from
Kano's Happosui Army.

458
00:26:37.090 --> 00:26:41.420
I heard that the old warrior Chin
Jao stepped down not too long ago.

459
00:26:41.420 --> 00:26:44.320
He did. That man's the new leader.

460
00:26:44.320 --> 00:26:46.180
Hiya, Sai!

461
00:26:46.180 --> 00:26:50.350
Hey, brother! I didn't think I'd
see you here, too, Leo!

462
00:26:50.350 --> 00:26:51.980
I'm a secret bodyguard!

463
00:26:51.980 --> 00:26:55.230
What a reliable ally!

464
00:26:55.230 --> 00:26:56.650
Agreed!

465
00:26:56.650 --> 00:26:58.480
Is he a friend of yours?

466
00:26:58.480 --> 00:27:01.990
Yeah, and we exchanged cups
of saké with Luffyland together!

467
00:27:02.240 --> 00:27:03.870
-Hey, Leo. -Huh?

468
00:27:03.870 --> 00:27:07.450
Listen. I'm doing my part and
working hard for the Kingdom of Kano,

469
00:27:07.450 --> 00:27:11.290
but after this bodyguard job
is done, I'm cutting ties.

470
00:27:11.290 --> 00:27:14.500
When I make a vow,
I don't take it lightly.

471
00:27:14.790 --> 00:27:17.800
I owe a great debt to the
Straw Hats after they saved me,

472
00:27:17.800 --> 00:27:19.760
and I intend to pay it back.

473
00:27:20.300 --> 00:27:23.570
All seven representatives
of the Straw Hat Fleet,

474
00:27:23.570 --> 00:27:29.860
along with all 5,600 of our troops,
have to be ready to aid him at any time.

475
00:27:31.990 --> 00:27:35.740
I heard the other members
have started preparing as well.

476
00:27:42.690 --> 00:27:44.160
What is this?

477
00:27:43.310 --> 00:27:44.100
<b>Resignation</b>

478
00:27:44.160 --> 00:27:48.200
You think you can resign from
the Standing Kingdom just like that?

479
00:27:44.730 --> 00:27:45.190
<b>Resignation</b>

480
00:27:48.200 --> 00:27:49.910
Tell me why!

481
00:27:49.910 --> 00:27:52.830
Forgive me, but there's
a debt I must repay.

482
00:27:52.830 --> 00:27:56.660
Barrier! Barrier Crash!

483
00:27:57.140 --> 00:27:58.640
Stay behind the barrier and

484
00:28:00.530 --> 00:28:02.890
cross your fingers for good luck!

485
00:28:02.890 --> 00:28:05.480
That's my battle-tested
secret for success!

486
00:28:05.480 --> 00:28:08.810
We surrender!
Please, just show us mercy!

487
00:28:08.810 --> 00:28:10.440
We'll even serve under you!

488
00:28:10.440 --> 00:28:12.780
Whatever you want!

489
00:28:14.010 --> 00:28:15.300
Good. Then put this on.

490
00:28:16.670 --> 00:28:18.050
What is it?

491
00:28:19.840 --> 00:28:23.510
Wear this and show your support
for the Straw Hats with us!

492
00:28:23.780 --> 00:28:24.990
– Do it!
– Do it!

493
00:28:28.810 --> 00:28:31.900
Two unidentified ships
are approaching, sir!

494
00:28:32.170 --> 00:28:35.750
Here to avenge Doflamingo?

495
00:28:35.750 --> 00:28:37.090
What, Cavendish?

496
00:28:37.090 --> 00:28:39.880
Oh, it's nothing like that.

497
00:28:39.880 --> 00:28:44.170
I was the prince of the Bourgeois
Kingdom, as you may already know.

498
00:28:44.170 --> 00:28:48.890
Prince Cavendish!

499
00:28:48.890 --> 00:28:54.140
Naturally, all the women in the kingdom
were absolutely crazy about me.

500
00:28:54.140 --> 00:28:57.180
They refused to marry
any man other than myself.

501
00:28:57.180 --> 00:28:59.720
And so, I was expelled
from the kingdom,

502
00:28:59.720 --> 00:29:03.310
charged with the crime
of being too popular.

503
00:29:03.310 --> 00:29:05.230
So in other words...

504
00:29:05.230 --> 00:29:09.240
The ships pursuing us are not
enemies, but my adoring fans.

505
00:29:12.910 --> 00:29:16.620
I know there's people even
stronger than Doflamingo out there.

506
00:29:16.620 --> 00:29:20.120
And I'm sure that Straw Hat will
face many of them in combat.

507
00:29:20.120 --> 00:29:23.550
If we want to help, we must
build our own strength, too.

508
00:29:23.550 --> 00:29:24.710
Agreed!

509
00:29:24.710 --> 00:29:27.340
My crew and I are
training hard every day!

510
00:29:27.340 --> 00:29:31.680
And I hope we can fight
together by Luffyland's side!

511
00:29:31.680 --> 00:29:33.120
Right!

512
00:29:37.960 --> 00:29:40.470
Well, if it isn't Princess Vivi!

513
00:29:41.630 --> 00:29:42.680
Wapol!

514
00:29:43.220 --> 00:29:46.850
<b>King Wapol
Evil Kingdom of Black Drum</b>

515
00:29:45.050 --> 00:29:46.310
You fool!

516
00:29:47.140 --> 00:29:49.520
<b>Queen Kinderella
Evil Kingdom of Black Drum</b>

517
00:29:49.810 --> 00:29:51.650
What's a goon like you doing here?

518
00:29:51.650 --> 00:29:58.190
A fine question!
I have Straw Hat to thank!

519
00:29:58.190 --> 00:30:01.660
He sent me flying away
to a strange and distant land!

520
00:30:01.660 --> 00:30:04.280
But I'm back, baby! And in charge!

521
00:30:04.280 --> 00:30:08.410
So, you fools, wanna know how
my darling rose to power again?

522
00:30:08.410 --> 00:30:09.580
What a coincidence!

523
00:30:09.580 --> 00:30:12.130
They must be friends
of Luffy's as well!

524
00:30:12.130 --> 00:30:14.920
Not quite. He's an enemy.

525
00:30:14.920 --> 00:30:19.720
That old fuddy-
duddy King Cobra doing well?

526
00:30:19.720 --> 00:30:22.760
Actually, I know he's not doing well.

527
00:30:22.760 --> 00:30:24.050
I saw him earlier.

528
00:30:24.050 --> 00:30:27.470
I was making a joke
at your expense.

529
00:30:27.470 --> 00:30:29.760
Oh darling, you're the best!

530
00:30:29.760 --> 00:30:32.050
I really gold-dig your humor!

531
00:30:32.050 --> 00:30:35.940
You're the funniest man
in the universe!

532
00:30:37.520 --> 00:30:40.020
Wapol!

533
00:30:40.020 --> 00:30:42.520
That's enough of your jokes.

534
00:30:42.520 --> 00:30:45.320
It's sickening that
you came to power again.

535
00:30:43.990 --> 00:30:48.240
<b>King Dalton
Sakura Kingdom</b>

536
00:30:45.320 --> 00:30:48.530
I feel sorry for whatever
country you rule.

537
00:30:50.160 --> 00:30:52.410
The World
Government should be ashamed!

538
00:30:50.540 --> 00:30:55.790
<b>Dr. Kureha
Sakura Kingdom</b>

539
00:30:52.700 --> 00:30:55.830
They've got no standards
if they let you back in!

540
00:30:56.210 --> 00:30:58.500
Dalton! And that witch!

541
00:30:58.500 --> 00:31:00.380
H-How are you still alive?

542
00:31:00.670 --> 00:31:02.640
Asking about my beauty regimen?

543
00:31:02.640 --> 00:31:04.310
Not a chance!

544
00:31:04.310 --> 00:31:06.230
Dalton! Doctor Kureha!

545
00:31:06.230 --> 00:31:07.940
So nice to see you again!

546
00:31:07.940 --> 00:31:11.420
Hello, Vivi. You're looking
more regal than ever.

547
00:31:11.420 --> 00:31:14.360
Are you happy?

548
00:31:14.360 --> 00:31:18.820
If I'd known you were a princess back then,
I would've stuck you with a higher bill,

549
00:31:18.820 --> 00:31:20.910
that's for darn sure.

550
00:31:20.910 --> 00:31:22.500
Who are these two?

551
00:31:22.500 --> 00:31:24.210
They're friends from
a snow-covered island

552
00:31:24.210 --> 00:31:26.790
that I traveled to with Luffy
and the other Straw Hats.

553
00:31:30.300 --> 00:31:34.300
While we were on our way to Alabasta,
Nami suddenly fell ill.

554
00:31:34.300 --> 00:31:36.220
We needed to find a doctor.

555
00:31:36.220 --> 00:31:39.620
So we stopped on the
nearest inhabited island.

556
00:31:42.550 --> 00:31:47.760
Dalton helped Luffy get rid of Wapol and
became a bit of a hero to the kingdom.

557
00:31:47.760 --> 00:31:49.850
So he was appointed as king,

558
00:31:49.850 --> 00:31:53.690
and the Drum Kingdom was reborn
as the Cherry Blossom Kingdom.

559
00:31:53.690 --> 00:31:56.340
That's lovely.

560
00:31:56.340 --> 00:31:58.260
Hey, hey, hey!

561
00:31:58.260 --> 00:32:00.050
You're getting a real big head!

562
00:32:00.050 --> 00:32:04.600
Perhaps I need to remind you,
you're still my subordinate!

563
00:32:04.600 --> 00:32:07.390
Those days have long since passed.

564
00:32:07.390 --> 00:32:09.520
Now.

565
00:32:13.300 --> 00:32:14.840
I've become a king.

566
00:32:14.840 --> 00:32:17.010
I won't bow to you.

567
00:32:17.700 --> 00:32:19.030
Sweetie!

568
00:32:19.030 --> 00:32:22.020
Wow, Dalton! You're acting
like royalty already!

569
00:32:22.020 --> 00:32:22.920
You are a natural!

570
00:32:22.920 --> 00:32:24.370
Huh? C'mon.

571
00:32:25.850 --> 00:32:29.440
Listen up, Dalton!
You useless goody-two-shoes!

572
00:32:29.440 --> 00:32:33.630
If you wanna make it as a ruler,
you gotta get your hands dirty!

573
00:32:33.630 --> 00:32:36.590
I clawed my way back
to the top making a fortune

574
00:32:36.590 --> 00:32:39.730
with my Munch-Munch powers,
and trust me, I'd know!

575
00:32:39.730 --> 00:32:43.940
The higher up you climb, the sooner
you'll see this whole world is corrupt!

576
00:32:43.940 --> 00:32:46.870
That tip was free,
but the next one will...

577
00:32:46.870 --> 00:32:50.830
Oh, and by the way, did you
read the article on Luffy?

578
00:32:50.830 --> 00:32:52.670
Yes. From top to bottom.

579
00:32:52.670 --> 00:32:54.460
Oh. I get it!

580
00:32:54.460 --> 00:32:55.660
You're like us!

581
00:32:55.660 --> 00:32:56.790
Huh?

582
00:32:56.790 --> 00:32:58.590
Lucy's fan!

583
00:32:58.590 --> 00:33:00.800
Be honest, you like Luffyland, don'cha?

584
00:33:04.840 --> 00:33:05.880
He's the best.

585
00:33:07.300 --> 00:33:08.640
I thought so!

586
00:33:10.650 --> 00:33:14.950
The Underwater Prison, Impel Down.

587
00:33:11.970 --> 00:33:16.220
<b>Impel Down
The Undersea Prison</b>

588
00:33:21.370 --> 00:33:25.080
The bottom floor, Level 6,
holds the most dangerous criminals

589
00:33:25.080 --> 00:33:26.580
the world has ever known.

590
00:33:26.580 --> 00:33:31.000
It's called the Infinite Hell.

591
00:33:36.680 --> 00:33:39.480
Putting me in solitary, are you?

592
00:33:39.480 --> 00:33:41.150
I'm so lonely!

593
00:33:41.150 --> 00:33:43.180
Why, Magellan?

594
00:33:43.180 --> 00:33:48.060
Or is this a plot to protect me, maybe?

595
00:33:48.060 --> 00:33:52.230
Is there
an assassin from on high,

596
00:33:52.230 --> 00:33:53.700
out to kill me?

597
00:33:53.700 --> 00:33:54.950
Of course!

598
00:33:54.950 --> 00:33:57.120
I better watch my loose tongue!

599
00:33:57.120 --> 00:33:59.330
What a rotten mess I could cause!

600
00:33:59.330 --> 00:34:00.210
Just think.

601
00:34:00.210 --> 00:34:03.040
What if I told the whole world
the secret Mary Geoise is hiding?

602
00:34:08.590 --> 00:34:11.460
Why does it matter
if it's revealed now?

603
00:34:11.460 --> 00:34:13.760
Power doesn't last long.

604
00:34:13.760 --> 00:34:16.510
It'll rot faster than anyone thinks!

605
00:34:19.200 --> 00:34:22.460
<b>Mary Geoise</b>
